{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "godunov_norm_2d_eikonal_mms",
    "description": "Method-of-manufactured-solutions order-of-accuracy driver for grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/godunov_norm_D2_periodic on the doubly-periodic unit box [0,1]x[0,1], the 2-D companion of problems/godunov_norm_1d_eikonal_mms.esm. Forced-steady eikonal / Hamilton-Jacobi equation u_t = -S|grad u| + S|grad g| with the manufactured solution g(x,y) = sin(2 pi x) + sin(2 pi y): because u_t = -S|grad g| + S|grad g| = 0, g is the EXACT solution of the continuous forced PDE for all t (both the initial condition and the steady state), so the analytic reference at every time is g itself. The forcing S|grad g| = 2 pi S sqrt(cos^2(2 pi x) + cos^2(2 pi y)) is the constant-in-time source that balances the operator. Discretely u_t = S*(|grad g| - godunov(u)); starting from u(0) = g the imbalance is exactly the first-order truncation error S*(|grad g| - godunov(g)) = O(dx + dy), so the discrete solution drifts from g at rate O(h) and the L2 / Linf error at the assert time falls as O(h) \u2014 expected order 1. THE KINKS ARE NOT A PROBLEM: |grad g| has slope-sign kinks where each gradient component g_x = 2 pi cos(2 pi x), g_y = 2 pi cos(2 pi y) changes sign (x,y = 1/4, 3/4) and a norm cusp where grad g vanishes, yet the Godunov / Rouy-Tourin / Osher-Sethian entropy fix sqrt(max(D-,0)^2 + min(D+,0)^2) selects the correct one-sided branch per axis through the kink, so the scheme retains clean first-order accuracy in L2 AND Linf uniformly (numerically verified: pairwise orders 0.99 -> 1.00 in both norms across NX=NY = 16..128). This is the property that distinguishes the Godunov norm from a naive centered |grad u| and the reason a doubly-periodic sin MMS \u2014 whose gradient components necessarily change sign \u2014 still converges at order 1. Both g and |grad g| are doubly periodic (g(0,y)=g(1,y), g(x,0)=g(x,1); |cos| has period 1/2), so the periodic wrap is fully consistent (no seam artifact), unlike a non-periodic ramp; the wrap faces converge at the same order-1 rate as the interior, so the state L2/Linf reduction over the whole field is a clean order-1 gate with nothing to exempt. The grid's consumer-supplied geometry contract (grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/grid.esm) is fulfilled for the unit box: x0=y0=0 and dx=1/NX, dy=1/NY (observeds dividing the extent by the metaparameter names, esm-spec 9.7.6, so the loader-API rebinding of NX,NY for the convergence sweep keeps dx,dy consistent). The ic, the forcing observed, and the test reference spell the cell-center coordinates x_i = (i - 1/2)/NX, y_j = (j - 1/2)/NY inline from literals and the metaparameters NX,NY (the build-time cellwise evaluation is scope-free; build-time coordinate expressions fold from literals and NX,NY alone, never the free-name x_coord/y_coord templates). Per-resolution error norms are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/godunov_norm_2d_eikonal_mms/golden/errors.json.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "equation:hamilton_jacobi",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Rouy, E., & Tourin, A. (1992). A viscosity solutions approach to shape-from-shading. SIAM Journal on Numerical Analysis, 29(3), 867-884. Convergence of the monotone Godunov Hamiltonian sqrt(sum_d max(D-,0)^2 + min(D+,0)^2) to the viscosity solution of the eikonal equation at first order.",
        "doi": "10.1137/0729053"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Osher, S., & Sethian, J. A. (1988). Fronts propagating with curvature-dependent speed: Algorithms based on Hamilton-Jacobi formulations. Journal of Computational Physics, 79(1), 12-49. The upwind entropy construction of |grad phi| for level-set Hamilton-Jacobi terms.",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(88)90002-2"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "GodunovEikonal2DMMS": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/godunov_norm_D2_periodic.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "x",
            "y"
          ],
          "description": "Level-set field integrated under the forced eikonal u_t = -S*godunov(u) + S|grad g|; starts at and stays near the manufactured solution g(x,y) = sin(2 pi x) + sin(2 pi y), deviating by the O(h) truncation error."
        },
        "S": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Non-negative Hamilton-Jacobi speed (u_t = -S|grad u|). The forcing carries the matching S so g is the exact steady solution for any S > 0."
        },
        "x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Left x domain edge a = 0 (unit box): the grid's x0 free name (consumer-supplied geometry contract, grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/grid.esm)."
        },
        "y0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Bottom y domain edge b = 0 (unit box): the grid's y0 free name."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "m",
          "expression": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              1,
              "NX"
            ]
          },
          "description": "x-spacing 1/NX: the grid's dx free name, resolved inside the rewrite rule's expanded body at evaluation. NX is the document-scoped metaparameter, substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6), so loader-API rebinding for the convergence sweep keeps dx consistent."
        },
        "dy": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "m",
          "expression": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              1,
              "NY"
            ]
          },
          "description": "y-spacing 1/NY: the grid's dy free name; NY substituted at load so the sweep keeps dy consistent."
        },
        "forcing": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1/s",
          "shape": [
            "x",
            "y"
          ],
          "description": "The manufactured source S|grad g| = 2 pi S sqrt(cos^2(2 pi x_i) + cos^2(2 pi y_j)), a spatially varying constant-in-time field (S folded via the du/dt scaling; here the |grad g| factor, x_i = (i - 1/2)/NX, y_j = (j - 1/2)/NY spelled inline). It exactly balances the continuous operator so g = sin(2 pi x) + sin(2 pi y) is the steady exact solution; the residual after discretization is the O(h) truncation error.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "i",
              "j"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "x"
              },
              "j": {
                "from": "y"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                6.283185307179586,
                {
                  "op": "sqrt",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "+",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "^",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "cos",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "*",
                                  "args": [
                                    6.283185307179586,
                                    {
                                      "op": "*",
                                      "args": [
                                        {
                                          "op": "-",
                                          "args": [
                                            "i",
                                            0.5
                                          ]
                                        },
                                        {
                                          "op": "/",
                                          "args": [
                                            1,
                                            "NX"
                                          ]
                                        }
                                      ]
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            2
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "^",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "cos",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "*",
                                  "args": [
                                    6.283185307179586,
                                    {
                                      "op": "*",
                                      "args": [
                                        {
                                          "op": "-",
                                          "args": [
                                            "j",
                                            0.5
                                          ]
                                        },
                                        {
                                          "op": "/",
                                          "args": [
                                            1,
                                            "NY"
                                          ]
                                        }
                                      ]
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            2
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "ic",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "i",
              "j"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "x"
              },
              "j": {
                "from": "y"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "sin",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        6.283185307179586,
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "-",
                              "args": [
                                "i",
                                0.5
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "/",
                              "args": [
